# Material You UI

This project follows **Material You (Material Design 3)** for UI chrome,
with a **neutral charcoal / deep slate** workspace palette (Cases-style SaaS), not green-as-primary or purple-indigo.

## Brand palette (NSLAW workspace)

Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` (`:root` / `.dark`):

- `--primary` / `--action: #0f172a` (deep slate / charcoal) — main CTAs, Selected chips, `bg-primary` / `bg-action`
- `--primary-foreground` / `--action-foreground: #ffffff`
- `--primary-hover: #020617`
- `--primary-muted: #f1f5f9` — tonal containers, active nav, secondary buttons
- `--accent: #475569` (slate) + `--accent-muted: #f8fafc`
- `--canvas: #f8f9fa`, `--sidebar: #f3f4f6`, `--border: #e5e7eb`
- Radius: `--radius-md: 0.75rem` (12px); cards `--radius-lg` 16px
- CTA + filter chips: `rounded-full`; inputs/selects: `rounded-xl`
- Overlay shadow: `var(--shadow-overlay)` for modal/panel/menu

Logo mark (`public/logo-nslaw.png`) may still show **green + gold**; do not force those hexes as app primary unless the user asks.

